orts a modest Democratic edge with meaningful uncertainty in an open-seat battleground.", "watch": "The first debate and any further narrowing in late-October polls could shift this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open Senate seat features Democrat Abdul El-Sayed against Republican Mike Rogers, with incumbent Gary Peters retiring. Polling across more than a dozen surveys has El-Sayed ahead by roughly three points on average, though the most recent polls from early October show a much tighter race, with two putting the margin at a single point.\n\nExpert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets price El-Sayed's chances near 70%. Rogers benefits from stronger outside spending on his side, while El-Sayed has faced heavy outside opposition. The race remains competitive, with the first debate in early October a potential inflection point.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7248, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7315, "margin": 3.2}]}